      },
      {
        "id": "uniqueness",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Uniqueness of the factorization up to homeomorphism",
        "statement": "Any alternative continuous monotone-light factorization through a Hausdorff\nmiddle space, with surjective first map, admits a unique commuting homeomorphism\nfrom the component quotient. Uniqueness is on the carrier.",
        "informal_proof": "In any such factorization with surjective monotone first map and\nlight second map, a fibre of the first map is contained in an f-component.\nConversely, the image of an f-component is connected inside a light fibre and\nthus a singleton. Hence the first map has exactly the same fibres as q. The\nquotient lifting theorem supplies a continuous bijection of middle spaces,\nwhich is a homeomorphism by compactness and the Hausdorff condition.",
        "goal": null,
        "uses": [
          "factorization"
        ],
